#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119623 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119812 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3c3466c-dfb0-5b5f-b556-ce57a1d78519" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Whether a Vector Lies in the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "fe2f3934-fa5c-5a59-be7e-00b6e4889063" :question/math-academy-id "e-4810" :question/problem "The matrix $A$ and vectors $\\mathbf{b}_1$, $\\mathbf{b}_2$, $\\mathbf{b}_3$ are given below. Which of the vectors lie in $\\textrm{Null}(A)?$\n\n![](images/53/53e17b54ff077d45401bdc4754ccdcff5d0cad20e8d5b477b7a9e0aec37ab52c.svg)" :question/worked-solution "A vector $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Null}(A)$ if $A\\mathbf{b}=\\mathbf{0}.$ So, we need to compute the product of $A$ and each of the given vectors and check whether it is equal to $\\mathbf{0}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{b}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 \\\\ -5 & 10 \\\\ -8 & 16\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-27 \\\\ 45 \\\\ 72\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 \\\\ -5 & 10 \\\\ -8 & 16\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=0\\,✓ \\\\ A{b}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -6 \\\\ -5 & 10 \\\\ -8 & 16\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-15 \\\\ 25 \\\\ 40\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $\\mathbf{b}_2$ lies in $\\textrm{Null}(A).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119624 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119813 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9171c6fb-ad0b-538f-b982-a2502a20e253" :knowledge-point/title "Solve a Variable in a Vector Lying in the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "e38db5fa-1753-5176-bb5e-a077ea63ddec" :question/math-academy-id "e-4812" :question/problem "Consider the matrix ![](images/c8/c85268d7db6efb171da25432988c0ee99252f4cdb10f8a1cc24f31af5b2e239d.svg) and the vector ![](images/c7/c7095b22e7a8cbbeefc6b75b63886550a4c7c35f23585e2c0006ddf14b424c28.svg) Find the value of $k$ such that $\\mathbf{b}\\in\\textrm{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Null}(A),$ then we must have $A\\mathbf{b} = \\mathbf{0}.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 6 & -6 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ k \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}6+2k-12 \\\\ -6+3k-3 \\\\ 12-6k+6\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2k-6=0 \\\\ 3k-9=0 \\\\ -6k+18=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119625 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119814 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "465ce2b7-352e-5050-a5e4-0753fbacebf5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "1e59cd29-ea54-5b90-8215-60c81d1b6dbb" :question/math-academy-id "e-4814" :question/problem "Consider the matrix ![](images/17/17cd2f2b0846461e1ed6480f82ce576fc82e5066258d80ed6f7084b0d55ca4a9.svg) Find $\\textrm{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "We need to solve the equation $A\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -12 \\\\ 3 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{4}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe second equation tells us that $x_2=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2} & =0 \\\\ {x}_{1}-3(0) & =0 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that ![](images/db/db533ede6312d49204e619379dfff639c0871f37ee997ce152ec35bd64105926.svg) is the only solution to this system.\n\nTherefore, $\\textrm{Null}(A) = \\left\\{ \\mathbf{0} \\right\\}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186417741 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119813 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9171c6fb-ad0b-538f-b982-a2502a20e253" :knowledge-point/title "Solve a Variable in a Vector Lying in the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4345a24b-01f2-51a9-a9a3-ec26cb12faf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417717} {:answer/id #uuid "59f64036-7331-5cd3-843e-78a74738a9d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417719} {:answer/id #uuid "754f9b55-2a4f-56a1-a443-6730aeb9dbd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417721} {:answer/id #uuid "a602ff6b-6d7d-5c41-a3a4-a43d6175780c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417725} {:answer/id #uuid "d5fab15a-6aaa-5d52-a720-35f24b947f9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417731}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "754f9b55-2a4f-56a1-a443-6730aeb9dbd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417721} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b31ab65-a8d2-52bf-9fe7-84343a8c24b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417734}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "89126de9-6477-52ae-9bf6-a1ac2a8f4680" :question/math-academy-id "q-111103" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -12\\end{aligned}]$ and the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the value of $k$ such that $b\\in \\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then we must have $Ab=0.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -12\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}2k-6 \\\\ -k+3 \\\\ 4k-12\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2k-6=0 \\\\ -k+3=0 \\\\ 4k-12=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186417740 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119814 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "465ce2b7-352e-5050-a5e4-0753fbacebf5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29619f9b-9f06-5558-89f7-4d0e65e0b6fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417712} {:answer/id #uuid "7d97603e-1f0e-5a8d-be4f-823054e6c132" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}6{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417722} {:answer/id #uuid "8000a495-b4c4-55db-b5e6-b3a10f46cfdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ -{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{1}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417723} {:answer/id #uuid "88ca81a7-6293-5d02-80a7-1fbb2af96184" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417724} {:answer/id #uuid "aa0d38bc-db7b-538c-b0be-911380152f0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417726}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29619f9b-9f06-5558-89f7-4d0e65e0b6fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417712} :answer-field/id #uuid "59767641-5ff1-522d-98ff-ca8331e026ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417735}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "87edb91a-a643-5fdb-a1df-2e5d059d6b9b" :question/math-academy-id "q-111154" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -8\\end{aligned}].$ Find $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 0=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is ${x}_{1}$, and we have one free variable, ${x}_{2}.$ That means we need to find ${x}_{1}$ in terms of ${x}_{2}.$\n\nFrom the first equation we get ${x}_{1}=2{x}_{2},$ so the set of all the solutions of $Ax=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A)={[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186417742 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119814 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "465ce2b7-352e-5050-a5e4-0753fbacebf5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "267cb3d1-2ef0-50d2-827b-ba6571c4e7a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417711} {:answer/id #uuid "4c4607fe-b4f6-500f-b628-c9efb2f77b90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417718} {:answer/id #uuid "63a9c9e9-789b-5e69-a3e9-b68cbdaf3c6e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417720} {:answer/id #uuid "cbb639f6-eb5e-5bc1-a3ee-ebf239dfc56d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{1}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417730} {:answer/id #uuid "e3dcbb04-64eb-5c82-a9e6-1019c7c418e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]\\,:\\,{x}_{2}\\in R}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417732}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "267cb3d1-2ef0-50d2-827b-ba6571c4e7a7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{0}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417711} :answer-field/id #uuid "9debef96-eaa3-515c-b307-163bd264f5ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417736}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f53050dc-6a1d-553b-afc7-7c5bd1dcb5bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-111165" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}].$ Find $\\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "We need to solve the equation $Ax=0.$ First, we find the row echelon form of $A$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ {x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe second equation tells us that ${x}_{2}=0.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-3(0)=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=0.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that $x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$ is the only solution to this system.\n\nTherefore, $\\text{Null}(A)={0}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402362 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119812 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3c3466c-dfb0-5b5f-b556-ce57a1d78519" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Whether a Vector Lies in the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0957d54-3a75-5c9c-85ed-c3fc9e27319a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402364} {:answer/id #uuid "a07d906a-9817-56bc-a8bc-f84fb817ea22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402365} {:answer/id #uuid "ffba3c8a-b1b6-5ff8-95f5-61453383f036" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402366} {:answer/id #uuid "574e668b-516f-527f-a863-a5d86ad524ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{2}$ and ${b}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402367} {:answer/id #uuid "6b7c7a5a-0d78-5275-8321-8300ff247f49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0957d54-3a75-5c9c-85ed-c3fc9e27319a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{2}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402364} :answer-field/id #uuid "504c5c81-a875-5c21-b5d2-42ca7fdd3f22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402363}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cade4505-b877-5cb5-ae1c-bc1354365d4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-34361" :question/problem "The matrix $A$ and vectors ${b}_{1}$, ${b}_{2}$, ${b}_{3}$ are given below. Which of the vectors lie in $\\text{Null}(A)?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -10 & 8\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Null}(A)$ if $Ab=0.$ So, we need to compute the product of $A$ and each of the given vectors and check whether it is equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{b}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -10 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}41 \\\\ 82\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -10 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=0\\,✓ \\\\ A{b}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -10 & 8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 14\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only ${b}_{2}$ lies in $\\text{Null}(A).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186417738 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119813 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9171c6fb-ad0b-538f-b982-a2502a20e253" :knowledge-point/title "Solve a Variable in a Vector Lying in the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "065f9865-0513-58da-9b22-d96229767c84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417708} {:answer/id #uuid "2bc79277-ae90-5b10-b515-d4f65951b373" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417713} {:answer/id #uuid "2ecdee28-7a39-54e8-b845-add658821807" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417714} {:answer/id #uuid "ae95c44a-5b3c-5f86-ad5d-103a70a2b3df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417728} {:answer/id #uuid "c6656c99-3f58-5764-82e3-b277dcfb1731" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417729}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6656c99-3f58-5764-82e3-b277dcfb1731" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417729} :answer-field/id #uuid "035f7b17-da06-59f6-9265-6f52b45bcb1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417733}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3276f9dc-0fc5-5be4-8351-1b5347481225" :question/math-academy-id "q-34382" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -6\\end{aligned}]$ and the vector $b=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ k \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the value of $k$ such that $b\\in \\text{Null}(A).$" :question/worked-solution "If $b\\in \\text{Null}(A),$ then we must have $Ab=0.$ Substituting the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Ab & =0 \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ k \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}3+k+2 \\\\ 4+2k+6\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis corresponds to the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}k+5=0 \\\\ 2k+10=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand for each of these equations, we obtain $k=-5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186417739 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119812 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e3c3466c-dfb0-5b5f-b556-ce57a1d78519" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Whether a Vector Lies in the Null Space of a Given Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b313932-8a2d-5efe-9590-f6798ae0a9bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417709} {:answer/id #uuid "1839cd87-9807-5099-aa1b-8c59eca72147" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417710} {:answer/id #uuid "4200484a-68ef-5a68-826c-3f22c3f6744b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417715} {:answer/id #uuid "43348635-a4e0-572f-b730-392f51070b83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{1}$,  ${b}_{2}$, and ${b}_{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417716} {:answer/id #uuid "aac34498-7b04-5d6d-ae12-08f353104028" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${b}_{3}$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417727}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b313932-8a2d-5efe-9590-f6798ae0a9bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "None" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417709} :answer-field/id #uuid "e63daa46-8b3f-5be5-a899-eeb5be3faafc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186417737}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "840cf185-0fde-50bc-83f8-78075677882d" :question/math-academy-id "q-74858" :question/problem "The matrix $A$ and vectors ${b}_{1}$, ${b}_{2}$, ${b}_{3}$ are given below. Which of the vectors lie in $\\text{Null}(A)?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,{b}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A vector $b$ lies in $\\text{Null}(A)$ if $Ab=0.$ So, we need to compute the product of $A$ and each of the given vectors and check whether it is equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{b}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times  \\\\ A{b}_{3} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, none of the vectors lies in $\\text{Null}(A).$"}]}
